he appropriate irrigation interval.  \n\n- **Monitoring advice**  \n  1. Once the node is online, check soil‑moisture daily for at least three consecutive days to see the trend.  \n  2. Compare the observed moisture with the irrigation schedule for the identified crop stage (e.g., ~7 days interval during grand growth, ~10 days during tillering).  \n\n- **When to seek expert help**  \n  1. If the node cannot be re‑connected within 24 hours, contact the local IISR extension officer for on‑site moisture assessment.  \n  2. If after obtaining reliable data the moisture remains around 32 % and you are unsure whether to irrigate, request a field visit to confirm crop stage and water‑requirement needs.", "fact_check": "checked", "fact_check_seconds": 1.16, "groq_calls": [{"purpose": "rewrite", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 206, "completion_tokens": 91, "seconds": 2.83, "status": "ok", "seq": 1}, {"purpose": "answer", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "prompt_tokens": 1841, "completion_tokens": 868, "seconds": 2.47, "status": "ok", "seq": 2}, {"purpose": "fact_check", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 1245, "completion_tokens": 628, "seconds": 1.16, "status": "ok", "seq": 3}]}
